error[ffi_field_type]: `Ev.kind` is `ev_kind` in `fixedbugs-517-a-field-is-told-the-header-s-type-width-and-sign.h`, a signed 32-bit integer, not `u32` — clang read the header's struct and the field disagrees
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-517-a-field-is-told-the-header-s-type-width-and-sign.hero:14:9
     |
  14 |         kind: u32  #~ ffi_field_type
     |         ^^^^
  note: a group's `record` IS the header's struct (§4.19), so every field is at the header's own width and sign: correct `kind`, or name the header that spells `Ev` this way
  note: `ev_kind` names no width of its own, as an enumeration's is each platform's choice: this is its width and sign on this machine, and a field is declared at the header's own on every platform the program builds for
  fix (guess): declare `kind` with `i32`

